      "message": "fix(2d): keep Face rows clear of 'Do not touch' items\n\nA Face operation now takes protected faces and edges. At each level the\nfacer cuts its rows short at the cutter-centre keep-out of the protected\nitems (each tip height from the level up to the clearance plane), and it\nlinks over the keep-out at the clearance plane where a row is cut short\nor a row-end step would cross it. A level with no row left is skipped\nand noted; when no level is left, the operation is refused with the\nitems named. Without protected items the path is the same to the byte.\n\nFixes #3343\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
